# Requirements

### H1: Constant drive on c0 or c1 moves the body

WHEN c0 is held at 1 and all other channels at 0, THE system SHALL move the body by more than 0.05 m in x.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.05, 3.0]
label = "inside"
[prediction.when]
k = 0
```

Parameter k = index of the channel driven at 1 (others 0).

### H2: Constant drive on c3 moves the body forward

WHEN c3 is held at 1 and all other channels at 0, THE system SHALL move the body by more than 0.05 m in x.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.05, 3.0]
label = "inside"
[prediction.when]
k = 3
```

Trials: k=3 (c3=1), k=4 (c4=1), k=5 (c1=-1).

### H3: Oscillating a single channel produces net x travel

WHEN c0 alone is driven with a 1 Hz sine of amplitude 1, THE system SHALL move the body by more than 0.05 m in x.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.05, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
k = 0
f = 1.0
```

Trials: k selects which channel (0, 2, 3) gets sin(2 pi f t); f=1.

### H4: A phase-lagged travelling wave over all channels moves the body

WHEN all five channels are driven by sin(2 pi f t - i*ph) (channel i), THE system SHALL move the body by more than 0.1 m in x for one sign of ph.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
f = 1.0
ph = 1.2
```

Trials: (f, ph) = (1, 1.2), (1, -1.2), (2, 1.2).

### H5: Frequency of the travelling wave sets forward travel

WHEN the travelling wave (ph=1.2) is driven at 4 Hz, THE system SHALL move the body by more than 0.1 m in x.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
f = 4.0
ph = 1.2
```

Sweep f = 0.5, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12 at ph=1.2.
